      "sourceAndAdaptationBoundary": "The named measurement and residual-reactant balances are the official UCI teaching method. The identical dilute-acid matrix, matched blanks, multi-point calibration, presence-only bound and below-listed assessment controls are explicit SkillPilot AUTHOR adaptations, not reported UCI results. No equilibrium constant is requested. The source’s near-complete standard conversion is an approximation; calibration linearity alone cannot certify it.",
      "proposedAssessmentOnly": true,
      "allNumericalReadingsAreSynthetic": true,
      "ownExperimentPerformed": false,
      "actualLearnerPerformance": false,
      "HumanApproval": false,
      "HumanTrial": false,
      "chemicalModel": {
        "reaction": "Fe³⁺(aq) + SCN⁻(aq) ⇌ [Fe(NCS)(H₂O)₅]²⁺(aq); coordinated solvent omitted in the shortened 1:1 equation",
        "observedProduct": "The identified red-orange iron-thiocyanate complex absorption band, compared with the supplied reference spectrum; not redness alone.",
        "reactants": "Unbound reactant pools are inferred from known initial totals and the measured/upper-bounded product, within the stated dilute 1:1 model. They are not falsely described as two directly measured free-ion spectra.",
        "knownLimit": "Higher Fe(NCS)n complexes, Fe hydrolysis, chloride/other ligands, concentration-dependent absorptivity and changed ionic strength can invalidate the 1:1 balances or calibration transfer. Prescribed dilute SCN, excess Fe, dilute acid and no added chloride reduce these effects; spectral-shape/linearity controls are necessary, but do not prove every hidden species absent. If these assumptions are materially contradicted, withhold the free-reactant conclusion and investigate speciation instead."
      },
      "schoolConditions": {
        "setting": "Supervised school laboratory; instructor supplies verified ready-made stocks and carries out their chemical risk assessment. Alternatively use the entire synthetic fixture for interpretation; it earns no execution points.",
        "safety": "Goggles, protective coat and pipetting aid; no mouth pipetting, heating or concentrated acids. Teacher-prepared dilute acid and iron solutions only; KSCN is harmful. Collect all iron/thiocyanate solutions as designated laboratory waste. Stop on spills, incorrect stock or failed controls.",
        "temperatureC": 25,
        "temperatureToleranceC": 0.5,
        "sealedForObservation": true,
        "noSpeciesAdditionDuringOriginalStateMeasurement": true
      },
